 *
 * Debug-build devicetree overlay, applied automatically whenever debug.conf is
 * in EXTRA_CONF_FILE (see app/CMakeLists.txt).
 *
 * debug.conf sets CONFIG_PM=n, so the kernel tick is the Cortex-M SysTick
 * clocked from the 48 MHz MSI instead of LPTIM1 on the LSE crystal (release).
 * A free-running MSI was measured ~1.22 % slow on the bench, and every kernel
 * timeout (report cadence, LoRaWAN RX windows, retries) drifts with it. MSI PLL
 * mode lets the hardware trim the MSI continuously against the 32.768 kHz LSE,
 * so the debug kernel clock tracks the crystal like the release build.
 *
 * Not applied to release: its tick already runs from the LSE (LPTIM1), and the
 * MSI PLL mode has not been validated there across Stop2 entry/exit.
 */

&clk_msi {
	msi-pll-mode;
};
